        "jsCode": "// 1. Grab the Playlist ID (since all 100 items in this batch share the same one)\nconst playlistId = $input.first().json.id;\n\n// 2. Loop through the 100 items and format them into an array of strict Spotify URIs\nconst trackUris = $input.all().map(item => `spotify:track:${item.json.spotify_id}`);\n\n// 3. Return exactly ONE item containing the payload for the HTTP Request\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    playlist_id: playlistId,\n    uris: trackUris\n  }\n};"
